{%- comment -%}
  sections/store-location.liquid

  The last band on the homepage: after lada-band, before the footer.
  Where the shop physically is, as a map and as the building itself.

  This is the LIGHT homepage, not /pages/lada, so every value here
  resolves against the site tokens (--surface, --surface-alt, --text,
  --border, --radius-media). None of the --lada-* palette appears. A
  champagne hairline sitting directly above the footer would hand the
  whole shop to one label; Lada gets its one dark beat above and then
  the page comes back to the house of brands to close.

  THE PAIR SHARES A HEIGHT BY GEOMETRY, NOT BY LUCK. The shopfront
  photograph is a 740x1285 portrait of a four-storey building, sign at
  the top and the open shop at the bottom, so a landscape crop of it
  destroys the only thing it shows. So the photo column is a narrow
  portrait track whose width is derived from the shared height
  (see --store-pw in store.css) and the map takes whatever is left as
  a wide plate. Both are exactly the same height, neither is squeezed
  into the other's shape.

  Hours and the telephone have NO defaults, the same call as
  lada-house: inventing opening hours for a real shop on Civil
  Quarters Road sends somebody to a closed door. Each line appears the
  moment it is filled in and not before.

  Every part is optional and every empty state is a real layout. Clear
  the photograph and the map runs the full width; clear the map and
  the photograph centres at its own ratio instead of stretching into a
  letterbox; clear both and the section is still a correct, readable
  address block. There is no state that renders a grey box.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign heading = section.settings.heading | default: 'Come and see the cloth'

  comment
    Only a URL Google will actually serve inside a frame is allowed
    through. Everything else resolves to '' and the map column is not
    printed at all, because a blocked iframe is worse than no iframe:
    it is a box the right size and shape that never fills in.

    Three things had to be measured against the live service rather
    than assumed, and two of them contradicted the obvious guess.

    1. The Share panel hands over a whole <iframe> tag, not a URL.
       Pasted into a text field that becomes src="<iframe src=..."
       and nothing loads, so pull the real src back out.

    2. output=embed is what turns a maps URL into a frameable page,
       but ONLY on the query forms. www.google.com/maps?cid=... and
       ?q=... both 301 to /maps/embed?pb=... and render. The path
       form does not: /maps/place/Name/@lat,lng/... with
       ?output=embed glued on the end answers 200 with the whole
       Maps application and x-frame-options: SAMEORIGIN, so the
       browser refuses it. That path URL is the one in the address
       bar, which makes it the likeliest thing to be pasted, so it
       is rebuilt from its own @lat,lng into the q= form rather
       than decorated and hoped for.

    3. ftid= does not survive the embed redirect. The listing URL
       ...?ftid=0x3918c3c1715e6971:0xee004b05858f4a99&output=embed
       redirects to /maps/embed?pb=!1m0, an empty parameter block,
       and draws a blank world map with no marker on it. cid= is the
       same identifier in decimal (0xee004b05858f4a99 is
       17149789868114528921) and it does survive, so the default
       below is the cid form. ftid is still right for the directions
       link, which opens Maps proper rather than an embed.

    The https:// test guards all of it: the value ends up in a src
    attribute, so anything that is not a plain secure URL is dropped.
  endcomment
  assign map_raw = section.settings.map_src | strip_newlines | strip
  if map_raw contains '<iframe'
    assign map_raw = map_raw | split: 'src="' | last | split: '"' | first
  endif
  assign map_scheme = map_raw | slice: 0, 8
  assign map_src = ''
  if map_scheme == 'https://'
    comment
      Order matters. /maps/embed is Google's own embed output and is
      always frameable, so it wins outright. The /@lat,lng path form is
      tested BEFORE output=embed, because a path URL that already
      carries the parameter is still refused: the parameter is not what
      makes a page frameable, the /maps/embed redirect is, and the path
      form never redirects. Trusting output=embed there is what put a
      blank box on the page.
    endcomment
    if map_raw contains '/maps/embed'
      assign map_src = map_raw
    elsif map_raw contains '/@'
      assign map_pt = map_raw | split: '/@' | last | split: ','
      assign map_lat = map_pt[0] | strip
      assign map_lng = map_pt[1] | strip
      if map_lat != blank and map_lng != blank
        assign map_src = 'https://www.google.com/maps?q=' | append: map_lat | append: ',' | append: map_lng | append: '&output=embed'
      endif
    elsif map_raw contains 'ftid='
      comment
        Deliberately nothing. ftid is dropped by the embed redirect
        (see 3 above) and there is no way to turn it into cid in
        Liquid, so this renders no map rather than an empty one.
      endcomment
    elsif map_raw contains 'output=embed'
      assign map_src = map_raw
    elsif map_raw contains 'google.com/maps?' or map_raw contains 'google.com/maps/?'
      assign map_src = map_raw | append: '&output=embed'
    endif
  endif

  assign has_map = false
  if map_src != blank
    assign has_map = true
  endif

  assign has_photo = false
  if section.settings.image or section.settings.photo_asset != blank
    assign has_photo = true
  endif

  assign photo_alt = section.settings.image_alt | default: 'The Khan Jee Center on Civil Quarters Road, Sheikhupura, lit at dusk'

  comment
    ONE sizes STRING FOR BOTH BRANCHES, read straight off store.css so
    the two cannot drift apart when the grid is next adjusted.

      under 500      the photo is the column, so 100vw
      500 to 900     --store-pw caps it at 420px flat
      900 to 1400    the track is --store-h * .62, and --store-h is
                     clamp(430px,50vw,700px), so it is exactly 31vw
      1400 and up    --store-h is pinned at 700, so the track is
                     pinned at 434px and stays there for good

    The last stop is the one worth having. Without a ceiling a bare
    31vw asks a 1920 screen for 595px of a box that is 434 wide, and
    on a two-times display that is the difference between fetching the
    photograph and fetching it twice over.
  endcomment
  assign photo_sizes = '(min-width:1400px) 434px, (min-width:900px) 31vw, (min-width:500px) 420px, 100vw'

  comment
    The 420px render exists only for the photograph that ships with
    the theme, so it is offered only when that is the file being asked
    for. A srcset candidate that 404s is not skipped, it is chosen and
    then fails to paint, so a client who types his own filename gets
    one honest src instead.
  endcomment
  assign photo_file = section.settings.photo_asset
  assign photo_small = ''
  if photo_file == 'khanjee-storefront.webp'
    assign photo_small = 'khanjee-storefront-w420.webp'
  endif

  assign has_facts = false
  if section.settings.address != blank or section.settings.hours != blank or section.settings.phone != blank or section.blocks.size > 0
    assign has_facts = true
  endif

  comment
    A url setting cannot carry a default in the editor, so the fallback
    lives here. Same listing as the embed above, written as ftid rather
    than cid: this one opens Google Maps proper instead of a frame, and
    the ftid form is what the listing's own share link uses.
  endcomment
  assign dir_url = section.settings.directions_url | default: 'https://www.google.com/maps?ftid=0x3918c3c1715e6971:0xee004b05858f4a99'
  assign dir_label = section.settings.directions_label | default: 'Get directions'
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Both columns are captured and then printed in the chosen order, so
  the swap is a change of DOM order rather than a CSS `order` on a
  flex child. The map is a focusable iframe: reordering it visually
  while leaving it first in the source would put a keyboard user's tab
  stop on the opposite side of the screen from the box that lights up.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture col_map -%}
  {%- if has_map -%}
    <div class="store__map">
      {%- comment -%}
        No frameborder attribute: it is obsolete and the border is off
        in CSS. width/height are the sizes Google's own embed ships
        with, kept so the box is roughly right in the instant before
        the stylesheet applies.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <iframe
        src="{{ map_src | escape }}"
        title="{{ section.settings.map_title | default: 'Map showing Khan Jee Center, Civil Quarters Road, Sheikhupura' | escape }}"
        width="600" height="450"
        loading="lazy"
        referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture col_photo -%}
  {%- if has_photo -%}
    <figure class="store__photo">
      {%- if section.settings.image -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Never ask Shopify for more pixels than the source has: the
          cap is the picked image's own width, and the 700w candidate
          is only offered when the source can actually fill it.

          sizes comes from photo_sizes at the top of the file, which is
          derived from the stylesheet rather than measured once and
          left behind: the figures that used to be written out here
          (266px at 900, 384px at 1440) were taken when --store-h was
          620, and the clamp has been raised to 700 since.

          Keep every attribute on its own line with no Liquid tag
          between them. A whitespace-stripping comment tag placed in
          the middle of the tag welds the previous attribute's closing
          quote onto the next attribute name, and Liquid also reads a
          comment tag written out inside a comment as a nested block
          and then eats the rest of the file looking for its end.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign pw = section.settings.image.width -%}
        {%- if pw > 1200 %}{% assign pw = 1200 %}{% endif -%}
        <img src="{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: pw }}"
             srcset="{% if pw > 700 %}{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w,
                     {% endif %}{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: pw }} {{ pw }}w"
             sizes="{{ photo_sizes }}"
             width="{{ section.settings.image.width }}" height="{{ section.settings.image.height }}"
             loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             alt="{{ section.settings.image.alt | default: photo_alt | escape }}">
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The shipped asset is khanjee-storefront.webp at 740x1285. The
          box is sized by the stylesheet and the image is object-fit
          cover inside it, so if the client swaps in a file of another
          shape these two numbers only affect the reserved box before
          CSS lands, never the final crop.

          740 real pixels into a box that is 434 at its widest and 279
          at a 900 laptop was the whole file every time. The 420 render
          covers every one-times screen; the full file is still there
          for the two-times ones, which is what the pair is for.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <img src="{{ photo_file | asset_url }}"
             {% if photo_small != blank %}srcset="{{ photo_small | asset_url }} 420w,
                     {{ photo_file | asset_url }} 740w"
             sizes="{{ photo_sizes }}"
             {% endif %}width="740" height="1285" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             alt="{{ photo_alt | escape }}">
      {%- endif -%}
    </figure>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The id is fixed rather than a setting so that anything linking to
  #store-location keeps working after the client renames the heading.
  One band per page; it is not a preset anyone should add twice.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="store" id="store-location" aria-labelledby="store-h-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="store__head" data-reveal>
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="store__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="store__h" id="store-h-{{ section.id }}">{{ heading }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}
        <p class="store__sub">{{ section.settings.text }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if has_map or has_photo -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign pair_class = 'store__pair'
        if has_map and has_photo
          assign pair_class = pair_class | append: ' store__pair--duo'
          if section.settings.map_side == 'right'
            assign pair_class = pair_class | append: ' store__pair--photo-first'
          endif
        endif
      -%}
      <div class="{{ pair_class }}" data-reveal style="--d:80ms">
        {%- if section.settings.map_side == 'right' -%}
          {{ col_photo }}{{ col_map }}
        {%- else -%}
          {{ col_map }}{{ col_photo }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if has_facts or dir_label != blank -%}
      <div class="store__info" data-reveal style="--d:160ms">
        {%- if has_facts -%}
          <dl class="store__facts">
            {%- if section.settings.address != blank -%}
              <div class="store__fact">
                <dt>{{ section.settings.address_label | default: 'Address' }}</dt>
                <dd><address>{{ section.settings.address }}</address></dd>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if section.settings.hours != blank -%}
              <div class="store__fact">
                <dt>{{ section.settings.hours_label | default: 'Open' }}</dt>
                <dd>{{ section.settings.hours }}</dd>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if section.settings.phone != blank -%}
              <div class="store__fact">
                <dt>{{ section.settings.phone_label | default: 'Telephone' }}</dt>
                <dd><a href="tel:{{ section.settings.phone | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' | remove: '(' | remove: ')' }}">{{ section.settings.phone }}</a></dd>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Blocks, so the client can add a line the build never
              anticipated (parking, a Friday closure, a Ramadan
              timing) and put it where he wants it, without a
              developer and without a new setting.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.settings.value != blank -%}
                <div class="store__fact" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                  <dt>{{ block.settings.label }}</dt>
                  <dd>{{ block.settings.value }}</dd>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </dl>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The text link is not a nicety. An iframe is a poor keyboard
          target, it is the first thing a privacy extension or a
          corporate proxy blocks, and it is dead weight on a slow
          connection. This link is the route out to the real thing and
          it renders whether or not the embed does.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if dir_label != blank and dir_url != blank -%}
          <a class="store__dir" href="{{ dir_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <span>{{ dir_label }}</span>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                 stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Store location",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Sits at the end of the homepage. Link to it from anywhere with #store-location" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Sheikhupura" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Come and see the cloth" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Text",
      "default": "Every brand on this site is on the shelf in one building on Civil Quarters Road. Bring the shalwar kameez you like the fit of and we will cut to it." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Layout" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "map_side", "label": "Map goes on the",
      "options": [
        { "value": "left", "label": "Left, photograph right" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "Right, photograph left" }
      ],
      "default": "left",
      "info": "They stack on a phone, in this same order." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Map" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "map_src", "label": "Google Maps embed URL",
      "default": "https://www.google.com/maps/embed?origin=mfe&pb=!1m3!3m2!1m1!4s17149789868114528921",
      "info": "From Google Maps: Share, then Embed a map, then Copy HTML. Pasting the whole <iframe> tag works, we take the URL out of it, and so does the long /maps/place/ address from the browser bar. A maps.app.goo.gl short link does not, Google will not show those in a frame. Clear this field to hide the map." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "map_title", "label": "Map title",
      "default": "Map showing Khan Jee Center, Civil Quarters Road, Sheikhupura",
      "info": "Read out by screen readers in place of the map." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "directions_url", "label": "Directions link",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the Khan Jee Center listing on Google Maps." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "directions_label", "label": "Directions link label", "default": "Get directions" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Shopfront photograph" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Portrait, the building from the street. Hidden if both fields are empty." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "photo_asset", "label": "…or theme asset filename",
      "default": "khanjee-storefront.webp",
      "info": "Used only when no image is picked" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Alt text",
      "default": "The Khan Jee Center on Civil Quarters Road, Sheikhupura, lit at dusk",
      "info": "A picked image uses its own alt text if it has one." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Details" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "address_label", "label": "Address label", "default": "Address" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "address", "label": "Address",
      "default": "Khan Jee Center, Civil Quarters Road, Sheikhupura" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hours_label", "label": "Opening hours label", "default": "Open" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hours", "label": "Opening hours",
      "info": "NOT SET. Left blank deliberately, the line is hidden until real hours are supplied. Do not guess." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "phone_label", "label": "Telephone label", "default": "Telephone" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "phone", "label": "Telephone",
      "info": "NOT SET. Hidden until supplied. Include the area code." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "detail", "name": "Extra detail", "settings": [
      { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "default": "Parking" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "value", "label": "Text", "info": "The row is hidden while this is empty." }
    ]}
  ],
  "max_blocks": 4,
  "presets": [{ "name": "Store location" }]
}
{% endschema %}
